# Build output
node_modules
dist
# The marketing site is built from src/landing/ by `npm run build:landing`.
# The hand-written page that used to live here is archived at
# docs/legacy-landing.html.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash — a bare `landing` matches at ANY depth, which
# silently excluded src/landing/ too: the entire marketing site (its components,
# its images, robots.txt, the sitemap) was untracked, so `git status` stayed
# clean no matter what changed in it. Only the build output belongs here.
/landing

# Live SQLite database and backups
data

# Secrets and local overrides (.env.example is committed)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Router-generated WireGuard client profiles contain private keys.
/wireguard/wg_confs/*.conf

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# The design export downloaded from GitHub (a zip)
Land
